{
 "bio": {
  "lang": "en",
  "script": "Latn",
  "text": "Essayias Lesanu Bezabeh is an Ethiopian-born author and poet who has written extensively in Amharic, often focusing on themes of identity, healing, and the experiences of the Ethiopian diaspora. After living in exile for 30 years, his travel memoir Selasa Besost explores his return to Ethiopia and the emotional landscape of reconnecting with his motherland."
